    test(e2e): exercise #134 human-claim repair (real Pung/Chow/Kong/Hu + assert acceptance)

    Reverses the pass-only workaround now that main carries #135/#134: claimByClick
    clicks the highest-value REAL claim button (Hu>Kong>Pung>Chow) the server offers,
    and the 4-hand gate asserts the repair is EXERCISED, not merely present —
    realClaimsAttempted>=1 (a real claim clicked via DOM) AND realClaimsAccepted>=1
    (the server let the human act: Pung/Chow/Kong → world.hasExtraHandTile advances to
    a discard; Hu → the observer records the human winning). Read-only observation
    only; no WS updates / state mutation. Also adds a stall state-dump for diagnosis.

    ⚠️ CURRENTLY BLOCKED by a P0 regression I found while validating this: #135
    (8aaa37b) hangs human-vs-bots games — a human real claim (or even a bot Chow-no-
    tileIds fallback) wedges the hand server-side; main (ab3687d) is RED on exactly
    this. Filed #139 (backend claim/runtime owner). NOT pushed until #139 lands.

    Refs #122, #128, #134. Blocked-by #139.

    Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

